# Row-aware 3-way merge for the shared JSON registers.
#
# MEASURED, main @1b82ab7: these five files re-conflict every sibling PR, and the
# dominant mechanism is a shared header scalar rather than the rows —
# 74% of MANAGER-CHECKLIST.json conflict pairs and 67% of OPEN-PRS.json ones have
# BOTH sides bumping the same `updated_at`/`as_of` line. PR #10815's entire
# conflict was that one line.
#
# ⚠️ A MERGE DRIVER IS CLIENT-SIDE. Git runs it on `git merge` / `git rebase`
# LOCALLY, and ONLY after `scripts/ops/install_merge_driver.sh` has registered it
# in this clone's git config. GitHub's servers do NOT run custom merge drivers, so
# this does NOT make a `mergeable_state: dirty` PR auto-mergeable on GitHub — it
# removes the cost of resolving the conflict by hand, which is the measured
# consumer of manager time. Saying otherwise would be claiming a fix that is not
# there.
#
# The driver REFUSES (exit 1, markers left) on divergent same-id adds or edits and
# on delete-vs-edit. It never picks a winner. See scripts/ops/merge_json_register.py.
#
# ⚠️ SHIPPING IT IS NOT ARMING IT, AND FOR THE FIRST DAY NOBODY WAS ARMED. Measured
# 2026-09-03 (MI-94): `git config --get merge.jsonregister.driver` was EMPTY in a
# fresh clone, and nothing in the SessionStart hook, any skill, or CI ran the
# installer — so every session container merged these files the old way. Two
# sibling branches each appending one row conflicted in 4 of 4 registers un-armed
# and 0 of 3 armed. `scripts/ops/manager_preflight.py`'s `merge_driver` check now
# FAILS an un-armed clone and names the one-line remedy, so the gap is visible at
# the moment it costs something rather than after.
#
# ⚠️ AND THE DRIVER IS ONLY HALF THE PROBLEM. It resolves the TEXTUAL collision; it
# cannot see a SEMANTIC one — a branch filing new work under an id `main` already
# gave to something else is, to git, one changed value at one key, so the merge
# DELETES the existing row and reports success. `scripts/ci/check_register_ids.py`
# (`register-id-guard`) is that half, and it runs on every PR.

docs/claude/health-review-backlog.json      merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/OPEN-ITEMS.json                 merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/work/MANAGER-CHECKLIST.json     merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/work/SESSIONS.json              merge=jsonregister
docs/claude/work/OPEN-PRS.json              merge=jsonregister

# ── docs/claude/pending-pings.jsonl — merge=union, NOT merge=jsonregister ──
#
# This one is line-delimited JSON, not a JSON object, and the difference decides
# the driver. MEASURED 2026-09-05 against current origin/main @5eb59917, over the
# full population of five ping-carrying PRs whose conflict was observed
# 2026-09-04 (#10888 #10902 #10908 #10914 #10926), test-merged in throwaway
# worktrees with merge.jsonregister ARMED:
#
#     no mapping (today)   5/5 CONFLICT   both sides' text left in markers
#     merge=jsonregister   5/5 CONFLICT   ⚠️ AND THE PR'S ROW IS NOT IN THE FILE
#     merge=union          0/5 CONFLICT   both sides' rows present, read and verified
#
# ⚠️ jsonregister IS NOT MERELY INEFFECTIVE HERE, IT IS WORSE THAN NOTHING. It
# parses the whole file as ONE JSON document, so appended LINES read to it as
# disagreeing header scalars and it refuses — correct instinct, wrong file. On
# the pre-rescue control (base b95ac61f, main before #10974) it left 74 rows and
# NO conflict markers while the PR's ping row was absent from the file entirely:
# a `git add` on that path drops the ping silently. Today's bare conflict at
# least leaves both sides' text where a human can see it.
#
# ⚠️ THE UNION OBJECTION WAS TESTED, NOT ASSUMED. union resurrects deletions, and
# a drained ping could in principle be deleted. It is not: notify_on_pull.py's
# `_drain_pending_pings` LEAVES THE FILE IN PLACE and dedupes by line hash via
# runtime_logs/pending_pings_delivered.txt (gitignored, per-clone) — its docstring
# says this replaced the old truncate-in-a-follow-up-commit contract. Measured
# over the file's whole history: 94 commits touch it; 4 show deletions; 3 predate
# the dedupe contract (350cc391, 2026-05-06) and were that old contract; the only
# post-dedupe one (39e6cbe0) is a pure reflow — 22 lines removed, all 22 re-added
# byte-identical, 0 rows semantically gone. So in 90 post-contract commits,
# nothing has ever removed a row, and union has nothing to resurrect.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT UNION DOES COST, STATED RATHER THAN GLOSSED. If a row was hand-rescued
# onto main by value (as #10974 did for these five) and the PR carrying it later
# merges, union keeps BOTH copies: merging #10888 into current main yields 91
# lines / 90 unique, the night_shift_summary row duplicated byte-for-byte. That
# is one duplicate operator page, because the hash ledger suppresses repeats
# ACROSS drain passes but not WITHIN one — `_drain_pending_pings` never adds to
# `delivered` as it iterates, so two identical lines return two pings (measured).
# Filed as BL-20260905-PENDING-PINGS-WITHIN-PASS-DUPLICATE. A duplicate page is
# noise and recoverable; a dropped ping is loss and is not. That is the trade
# this line takes, deliberately.
#
# ⚠️ CLIENT-SIDE ONLY, same as the drivers above: this does not make a `dirty`
# ping PR auto-mergeable on GitHub. It removes the hand-rescue cost for whoever
# holds an armed clone. union is a git BUILT-IN, so unlike jsonregister it needs
# no installer and works in a clone that never ran install_merge_driver.sh.
docs/claude/pending-pings.jsonl             merge=union
